+# Stable approval and contribution reporting update — v2.5
+
+Recorded: 2026-10-10. Maintainer: Stephan A. Davis.
+
+The maintainer approved AUREN Core Specs v2.5 as Stable on the basis of publication preparation R1 and requested creation of the Stable package with updated release/status metadata and unchanged Core rules. The publication version and intended GitHub tag are `v2.5`; FC2 and R1 identify historical reviewed sources.
+
+In the same instruction, the maintainer requested complete reporting routes in CONTRIBUTING.md: a Code of Conduct reference, private conduct and sensitive safety contacts, the private GitHub vulnerability form with an email fallback, and these suggested subjects:
+
+- `AUREN Core — conduct concern`
+- `AUREN Core — safety concern`
+- `AUREN Core — security report`
+
+The project contact is `stephan@stephanadavis.de`. The change adds reporting guidance and does not amend operative Core behavior or contribution licensing. Only the reporting paragraph is expanded; the remaining CONTRIBUTING text and the other three adopted policies are preserved. The unchanged preparation-R1 changelog is retained as a plain-text `.md.txt` snapshot; its relative links describe its original repository-root location.
+
+This record documents the maintainer's instruction in the project conversation. A static validator checks the recorded scope and byte identity; it does not authenticate the maintainer, certify safety or prove external publication or deployment. No new model runs were performed.
+
+GitHub's reporting guidance: https://docs.github.com/en/code-security/how-tos/report-and-fix-vulnerabilities/report-privately . This guidance was read on 2026-10-10; administrators may create a draft advisory directly, and private vulnerability reporting is separate from SECURITY.md.
+
+Content: CC BY-SA 4.0. Copyright © 2026 Stephan A. Davis.
